{"id":"valid-parenthesis-string","title":"Valid Parenthesis String","difficulty":"Medium","pattern":"Greedy","tags":["Greedy","String","Stack","Dynamic Programming"],"companies":{"google":2,"meta":3,"amazon":2,"microsoft":1},"description":"A string `s` contains `'('`, `')'` and `'*'`. Each `'*'` may be interpreted as `'('`, `')'`, or an empty string. Decide whether there is some interpretation under which `s` becomes a **balanced** parenthesis string (every opening bracket closed by a later matching one, never a close without an open).","examples":[{"input":"s = \"()\"","output":"true"},{"input":"s = \"(*)\"","output":"true","explanation":"Treat * as empty."},{"input":"s = \"(*))\"","output":"true","explanation":"Treat * as '('."},{"input":"s = \")(\"","output":"false"}],"constraints":["1 <= s.length <= 100","s[i] is '(', ')' or '*'."],"hints":["Trying all 3^k interpretations is hopeless. Track a range instead: the minimum and maximum possible number of currently open brackets.","'(' adds 1 to both; ')' subtracts 1 from both; '*' subtracts 1 from the minimum and adds 1 to the maximum.","If the maximum ever drops below 0 there are too many ')' and you fail. Clamp the minimum at 0 (interpret surplus * as empty). Valid iff the minimum is 0 at the end."],"function":"checkValidString","signature":"def checkValidString(self, s: str) -> bool:","arg_types":{"s":"str"},"return_type":"bool","compare":"exact","tests":[{"input":{"s":"()"},"output":true},{"input":{"s":"(*)"},"output":true},{"input":{"s":"(*))"},"output":true},{"input":{"s":")("},"output":false},{"input":{"s":"*"},"output":true},{"input":{"s":"(((**"},"output":false},{"input":{"s":"((*)"},"output":true},{"input":{"s":"**(("},"output":false},{"input":{"s":"(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*(*